## goal
Create approved self-contained Pi skill for Renovacion at `.pi/skills/renovacion/`, with all runtime resources, path-stable wrappers, and tests proving Pi-discoverable structure, skill-local execution, no repository-root dependency, and outputs under skill-local `proyectos/[id]/`.

Also create:
- design doc: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-25-self-contained-renovacion-skill-design.md`
- implementation plan: `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-25-self-contained-renovacion-skill.md`

## assumptions
- Approved scope is final: self-contained Pi skill only; no final README install instructions.
- `pdd/self-contained-renovacion-skill/explore` is source evidence. `pdd/self-contained-renovacion-skill/requirements` file is absent; user-provided approved scope is requirement source.
- Root engines remain source to copy from, but implementation should not redesign engine internals.
- Skill-local commands may use `uv`, Python 3.13, Bash, and Node.js.
- Since an Engram CLI exists, this plan is saved both as repository artifact `pdd/self-contained-renovacion-skill/plan` and via `engram save` with title/topic key `pdd/self-contained-renovacion-skill/plan`.

## constraints
- TDD required: builders must write failing tests before implementation for each functional slice.
- No production implementation in planning phase.
- Do not modify root `README.md` with install instructions.
- Preserve `proyectos/[id]/` convention for every created/saved project file.
- Keep all skill implementation files under `.pi/skills/renovacion/`.
- Pi skill frontmatter must include `name: renovacion` matching parent directory and non-empty `description`.
- Avoid Jest or new Node test framework; use Python subprocess tests and existing Node runtime.

