## validation strategy
- TDD tests first for each slice:
  - `test_skill_structure.py`
  - `test_python_wrappers.py`
  - `test_memory_wrapper.py`
  - `test_no_repo_root_dependency.py`
- Main acceptance commands:
  - `python .pi/skills/renovacion/scripts/validate-skill-structure.py`
  - `uv run --project .pi/skills/renovacion pytest -q .pi/skills/renovacion/tests`
  - `bash .pi/skills/renovacion/scripts/run-project.sh 1`
  - `git diff -- README.md`
- Expected final behavior:
  - Pi-discoverable frontmatter passes.
  - Skill-local resource presence passes.
  - Calc/spec/memory outputs are under `.pi/skills/renovacion/proyectos/1/`.
  - Temp-copy run passes outside repo.
  - No caller-cwd `proyectos/` output is created.
  - `README.md` unchanged.

## rollback or mitigation notes
- If copied resources create unexpected drift, recopy required files from root and rerun structure tests; do not refactor engines.
- If `run-spec.py` fails imports, keep directory name `lib/spec-engine` and fix importlib package alias only.
- If memory output path escapes skill root, fix `run-memory.sh` `cd "$SKILL_ROOT"` and explicit `PROJECT_PATH` before touching memory engine code.
- If tests depend on network logos, rely on committed `proyectos/1/assets/` fixture and existing placeholder behavior.
- If `uv run --project` behavior conflicts with workspace root, run from skill root with `cd .pi/skills/renovacion && uv run pytest -q tests` as fallback, then document exact successful command.

## handoff instructions for builders
- Use implementation plan `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-25-self-contained-renovacion-skill.md` for exact file contents, code blocks, commands, expected failures, expected passes, and commit checkpoints.
- Keep build groups file-isolated; do not have two builders edit same test/script file.
- Start each group by writing/running its failing test.
- Do not edit root `README.md`.
- Do not implement production changes outside `.pi/skills/renovacion/`.
- Preserve numeric `proyectos/[id]/` convention everywhere.

## risks and dependencies
- Pi discovery risk: invalid frontmatter or mismatched parent/name prevents skill load.
- Path risk: memory runner/assets use cwd, so wrapper cwd control is mandatory.
- Import risk: hyphenated `lib/spec-engine` breaks normal package imports; importlib alias is mandatory.
- Dependency risk: root pyproject lacks `jsonschema`; skill-local `pyproject.toml` must include it.
- Asset risk: missing catalog images may render placeholders; include fixture extractor images and verify smoke content.
- Scope risk: builders may add README install docs or PDF promises; reviewers must reject these.
